# B1 çalışma: ek örnek cevaplar (yazma) ve süreyi dolduran konuşma örnekleri
L2='Örnek 2 · farklı fikirlerle'
L3='Örnek 3 · daha zengin dil (B2\'ye yakın)'
W={
'b1w1':[(L2,'Hi Alex,\nGreat news about the sports club! Of course I\'ll come with you on Saturday – I\'ve wanted to try something new for a while.\nI\'d rather play tennis than go swimming. I swim every week at school, so tennis would be a nice change, and I\'ve got my brother\'s old racket.\nCould we meet at 9.30 at the bus stop near your house? Then we can walk to the club together.\nI\'m afraid I can\'t have lunch with you, because it\'s my grandmother\'s birthday and the whole family is eating together at one o\'clock. Maybe next time!\nSee you on Saturday,\nCan'),
 (L3,'Hi Alex,\nThanks for your message – I\'m really pleased you\'ve found a club you like, and I\'d love to come along on Saturday.\nTo be honest, I\'d prefer swimming. I hurt my wrist playing volleyball last month, and I don\'t think tennis would be a good idea until it\'s completely better.\nAs the club opens at nine, why don\'t we meet at quarter past outside the main entrance? That way we\'ll have plenty of time before it gets crowded.\nUnfortunately, I won\'t be able to stay for lunch, because I\'ve promised to help my dad move some furniture in the afternoon. Shall we go for a pizza another day instead?\nSee you soon,\nNehir')],
'b1w2':[(L2,'Dear Mrs Brown,\nThank you for telling us about the trip. Yes, I would definitely like to go!\nI think the class would enjoy the zoo more. We studied animals in science this term, and it would be great to see them in real life. Also, the zoo is outside, so we could have lunch in the park there.\nI suggest that we go by coach, because it\'s cheaper for a big group and we can all travel together.\nI would also like to visit the gift shop and buy some postcards for my little sister.\nBest wishes,\nEmre'),
 (L3,'Dear Mrs Brown,\nThank you for your email. I\'d be delighted to come on the class trip – it\'s a great way to end the term.\nIn my opinion, the science museum would be the better choice. Not only is it indoors, which is useful if it rains, but it also has a planetarium, which most of us have never been to.\nAs for travelling, I would suggest taking the train. The station is only five minutes from school, and it would be faster than a coach because there\'s always heavy traffic on the motorway.\nFinally, if there\'s time, it would be lovely to have a picnic in the gardens next to the museum.\nKind regards,\nIrmak')],
'b1w3':[(L2,'Cooking: my secret hobby\nMost of my friends are surprised when I tell them my favourite free-time activity is cooking. Every Sunday, I choose a recipe from the internet and make lunch for my family.\nI enjoy it because it\'s creative and the result is always delicious – well, almost always! It also helps me relax after a busy week at school.\nI think some hobbies are better alone, but cooking is more fun with other people. When my cousins visit, we cook together, and the kitchen is full of noise and laughter. Food tastes better when you share it!'),
 (L3,'Why I spend my weekends on two wheels\nIf you ask me how I prefer to spend my free time, the answer is simple: cycling. Every Saturday morning, I ride along the coast road with a small group from my neighbourhood.\nWhat I love most is the feeling of freedom. When I\'m cycling, I forget about exams and problems, and I notice things I would never see from a car or bus, like tiny beaches and old fishing boats.\nAlthough some people prefer to exercise alone, I think it\'s much more motivating to go with others. On cold mornings, I would probably stay in bed if my friends weren\'t waiting for me! So my advice is: find a hobby you love, and find people to share it with.')],
'b1w4':[(L2,'Technology: a useful tool, not a toy\nIn my class, we use laptops in most lessons, and sometimes we use our phones to take photos of experiments.\nTechnology helps me a lot. When I don\'t understand something, I can watch a short video about it, and online quizzes help me prepare for tests.\nHowever, phones can cause problems. Some students send messages during lessons or play games when the teacher isn\'t looking. I think phones should only be used when the teacher says so. Then they can be a great tool instead of a distraction.'),
 (L3,'Should phones be banned from classrooms?\nAt my school, we\'re allowed to use tablets in lessons, but phones must stay in our bags unless a teacher gives us permission.\nThere\'s no doubt that technology makes learning easier. We can look up information in seconds, practise vocabulary with apps and work on projects together online, even from home.\nOn the other hand, phones can be a serious distraction. It only takes one notification for a student to stop listening, and some people even use them to cheat in tests.\nIn my view, banning phones completely isn\'t the answer. Instead, schools should teach us how to use them responsibly – after all, we\'ll need those skills for the rest of our lives.')],
'b1w5':[(L2,'When the phone rang at midnight, Sam knew something was wrong. It was his neighbour, Mrs Clark, and she sounded frightened.\n"I can hear someone in my garden," she whispered.\nSam put on his shoes, took a torch and went next door. His heart was beating fast as he walked slowly around the house. Suddenly, he heard a noise behind the bins. He pointed his torch and saw two bright eyes looking at him.\nIt was a fox! It was eating the rubbish that the wind had knocked over. Sam laughed, and Mrs Clark made him a cup of hot chocolate to say thank you.'),
 (L3,'When the phone rang at midnight, Sam knew something was wrong. Nobody ever called him that late. He picked it up and heard his best friend, Leo, who was clearly upset.\n"I\'ve missed the last train home," Leo explained. "I\'m at the station and my wallet has been stolen."\nWithout hesitating, Sam grabbed his car keys. The streets were empty and it was raining heavily, so the journey took longer than usual. When he finally arrived, he found Leo sitting alone on a bench, wet and shivering.\nOn the way home, Leo kept apologising, but Sam just smiled. "That\'s what friends are for," he said. A week later, Leo surprised him with concert tickets to say thank you.')],
'b1w6':[(L2,'As soon as Elif opened her bag, she realised the key was missing. She had to open the school sports hall for the basketball team, and the match started in twenty minutes!\nShe ran back to the classroom and looked under her desk, but it wasn\'t there. Then she remembered that she had taken her bag to the canteen at lunchtime. She hurried there and asked the cook.\n"Is this yours?" the cook asked with a smile, holding up a small silver key.\nElif thanked her and ran to the sports hall. She opened the door just as the team arrived.'),
 (L3,'As soon as Elif opened her bag, she realised the key was missing. It was the key to her grandfather\'s old wooden box, which he had given her before he moved abroad, and she had promised to keep it safe.\nShe tried to stay calm and thought about everything she had done that day. She had been to the library, then to the park with her friends. Feeling worried, she went back to the park and searched every bench, but there was no sign of it.\nAs she was walking home, disappointed, a little boy ran up to her. "Did you drop this?" he asked, holding out the key. He had seen it fall from her bag and followed her.\nElif was so relieved that she bought him an ice cream. That evening, she put the key on a chain and wore it around her neck.')],
}
S={
'b1s1':[
 ["My name's Deniz Kaya, and I live in Eskişehir, a student city in the middle of Turkey. I live with my parents and my younger sister in a flat near the river.",
  "I'm Mert. I come from a small town near Bursa, but at the moment I live in Istanbul, because I'm studying there. I share a flat with two friends from university."],
 ["I'm a student. I'm in my last year at high school, so I'm studying very hard for the university exam. My favourite subjects are biology and chemistry.",
  "I work as a receptionist in a hotel. I've been there for two years. I like it because I meet people from different countries and I can practise my English."],
 ["I really enjoy playing basketball. I play with my friends in the park two or three times a week. I also like watching series in the evenings to relax.",
  "In my free time, I usually read novels or draw. I'm quite a quiet person, so I like hobbies I can do at home. At the weekend I sometimes go to art exhibitions."],
 ["My best friend is called Ayşe. We met on our first day at secondary school, and we've been friends ever since. She's very funny and honest, and she always listens to my problems. We love going to concerts together.",
  "My best friend's name is Tolga. He lives next door, so we see each other almost every day. He's really good at football and computers, and he's helped me a lot with my homework. We're planning a trip together next summer."],
 ["Last weekend I went to my cousin's wedding in Izmir. It was in a big garden by the sea, and there was lots of music and dancing. I didn't get home until two in the morning!",
  "Last weekend was quite quiet. On Saturday I tidied my room and did my homework, and on Sunday I went for a long walk with my dog in the forest. In the evening I watched a football match."],
 ["Next summer I'm going to work in a café near the beach, because I want to save money for a new laptop. If I have time, I'd also like to go camping with my friends.",
  "I'm going to visit my aunt in Germany next summer. I've never been abroad before, so I'm really excited. I'm hoping to see Berlin and maybe practise a bit of German."]],
'b1s2':[
 ["I usually go to school by bus. It takes about twenty-five minutes, so I listen to music or read on the way. When the weather's nice, I sometimes cycle instead.",
  "I walk to work, because my office is only fifteen minutes from my flat. I think it's a good way to start the day, and it means I don't have to worry about traffic."],
 ["I like lots of different music, but my favourite is rock. I love bands with loud guitars and good drummers. I also listen to Turkish pop when I'm with my friends.",
  "I mostly listen to jazz and classical music, because it helps me relax and concentrate when I'm studying. My parents listened to it a lot when I was a child."],
 ["I live in a flat on the fourth floor of a building in the city centre. It has three bedrooms, a small kitchen and a balcony where we have breakfast in summer. The best thing about it is the view of the mountains.",
  "My home is a small house with a garden in a quiet village. It's quite old, but it's very comfortable. My favourite room is the living room, because it has a big fireplace and we sit there together in winter."],
 ["My favourite food is mantı, a kind of Turkish pasta with meat and yoghurt. My grandmother makes the best mantı in the world, and it always reminds me of family dinners.",
  "I love sushi. I tried it for the first time two years ago and I loved it immediately. It's light and healthy, and there are so many different kinds to try."],
 ["Yes, I have. Two years ago I went to Greece with my family. We visited Athens and a small island. I loved the old buildings and the food, which was similar to Turkish food in many ways.",
  "No, I haven't been abroad yet, but I'd love to go to Japan one day. I'm really interested in Japanese culture, and I've been watching lots of videos about Tokyo."],
 ["Yes, it's very important for me, because I want to study at university abroad. English also helps me understand films, songs and websites, and I can talk to tourists in my city.",
  "English is important for my job, because many of our customers are from other countries. Also, I like travelling, and English helps me communicate wherever I go."]],
'b1s3':[
 ["I'd like to talk about the seaside promenade in my town. It's a long path next to the sea, near the city centre. In the evenings, especially in summer, it's full of people. Families walk with their children, young people ride bikes or skateboards, and older people sit on benches and chat. You can see fishing boats, seagulls and, at sunset, the sky turns orange and pink. You can hear the waves, music from the cafés and people selling corn and tea. I think people like it because it's free, it's close to the water and it's a relaxing place to meet friends after a busy day.",
  "One place that's very popular in my town is the central park. It's next to the old castle, so it's easy to find. At the weekend, families have picnics on the grass, children play in the playground and teenagers play football or volleyball. There's also a small lake with ducks, and people often feed them. You can hear children laughing, birds singing and sometimes a street musician playing the guitar. I think people love it because it's green and peaceful, and it's one of the few places where you can forget you're in a busy city."]],
'b1s4':[
 ["In this photo, I can see a busy train station, probably in the morning. There are lots of people walking quickly in different directions. On the left, a man in a dark suit is looking at his watch – I think he's late for work. In the middle, a young couple with big suitcases are checking the departure board, so maybe they're going on holiday. They look excited. On the right, a woman is buying a coffee from a small café. Most people are wearing coats and scarves, so it's probably cold outside. In general, people seem a bit stressed, because everyone is in a hurry.",
  "This photo shows the inside of a large station. It looks very modern, with a high glass roof. Near the front, a group of students with backpacks are sitting on the floor and laughing – maybe they're waiting for a school trip. Behind them, there's an old man holding a newspaper and looking at the trains. He looks relaxed. A mother is holding her little boy's hand, and he's pointing at a train. People are wearing summer clothes, like T-shirts and sunglasses, so I think it's a hot day. Most of them look quite happy and calm."]],
'b1s5':[
 ["Let's think about each idea. Joining a sports club is good because you meet people regularly and you have something to talk about. Taking an evening class is also useful, because people there are interested in the same subject. Volunteering is a great idea, because you help others and you work in a team. Using a social app is easy, but it can be a bit dangerous to meet strangers from the internet. Talking to neighbours is nice, but in big cities many people don't know their neighbours. In my opinion, the best way is joining a sports club, because you see the same people every week and it's easy to become friends.",
  "I'll start with the social app. It's probably the quickest way to find people with similar interests, but I'm not sure the friendships last. Talking to neighbours is friendly, but you might not have much in common. A sports club is great if you like sport, but some people don't. An evening class is a good choice because it's relaxed and you can talk during breaks. I think volunteering is the best idea, though, because you meet kind people, you feel useful, and working together on something important brings people closer."]],
'b1s6':[
 ["I prefer spending time with one or two close friends. In a big group it's difficult to have a real conversation, and some people don't get the chance to speak. With close friends, I can talk about anything, even my problems, and I feel more relaxed. But I think big groups are fun for parties or birthdays.",
  "I prefer big groups, because there's always someone to talk to and there's more energy. For example, when we go to the beach with ten people, we can play volleyball and lots of games. With only one friend, it can get boring after a while."],
 ["I think it's easier at school, because you see the same people every day and you do things together, like projects and sports. Online, it's easy to start chatting, but you don't really know if people are honest about themselves. Real friendship needs time together.",
  "In some ways, it's easier online. Shy people, like me, find it less stressful to write than to speak. Also, online you can find people who love the same things as you, even if they live far away. I met one of my best friends in an online game."],
 ["Today it's quite easy. You can send messages every day, share photos and have video calls. I talk to my cousin in Germany every Sunday on video. But I think it's also important to visit each other when you can, because meeting face to face is different.",
  "People can use social media to see what their friends are doing, and they can play online games together. Some people still send letters or postcards, which I think is very special. Planning a holiday together once a year is also a good way to stay close."]]}
